// ==============================================================================================
//                        S M C   O R D E R F L O W   F V G
// ==============================================================================================
//
//  Indicator Name : SMC OrderFlow FVG
//  Author         : Michael_Fx_Trader
//  Version        : v6.0 - July 2026
//  Pine Version   : Pine Script v6
//  Script Type    : Overlay indicator (plots on the price chart)
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  A U T H O R   V E R I F I C A T I O N   D E C L A R A T I O N
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  I am Michael_Fx_Trader, the publisher and sole original author of this exact implementation of
//  "SMC OrderFlow FVG." I designed the architecture of this tool, wrote every line of the Pine
//  Script v6 code contained in this file, tested it across multiple asset classes and timeframes,
//  and I take full and sole ownership and responsibility for it.
//
//  Specifically, I independently designed and coded: the three-candle fair value gap detection and
//  its ATR-relative minimum-size filter; the multi-timeframe request layer that finds gaps
//  independently on three configurable timeframes and maps them onto the chart; the six-factor
//  strength model built from displacement, delta alignment, relative volume, flow dominance,
//  middle-candle body and absorption, together with its tier classification; the confluence merge
//  that fuses overlapping gaps from different timeframes and awards a multi-timeframe bonus; the
//  mitigation engine with its touch, half-fill and full-fill modes; the per-zone flow bars and
//  statistics label; the estimated buy and sell volume split that feeds the delta throughout; the
//  Universal Activity engine that keeps the flow model alive on volume-less feeds; the complete
//  multi-section dashboard; and the alert framework.
//
//  This declaration is made for this specific version of the script (v6.0, July 2026). Any future
//  modified version I publish will carry its own updated declaration in this same header.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  O R I G I N A L   I N D I C A T O R   S C R I P T   I M P L E M E N T A T I O N
//  V E R I F I C A T I O N   A N D   D E C L A R A T I O N
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  I verify and declare that this script is an original implementation authored from scratch by
//  Michael_Fx_Trader. No portion of this code was copied, ported, decompiled, translated,
//  reverse-engineered or adapted from any other author's closed-source, invite-only, protected or
//  open-source script. No third-party library and no republished open-source script forms any part
//  of this work, and no other author's scoring model, dashboard layout or visual system was
//  reproduced.
//
//  I acknowledge openly that the underlying trading concepts are public and widely taught. The
//  fair value gap, the three-candle imbalance that defines it, the idea that a gap left by a fast
//  move represents inefficiency that price may return to fill, multi-timeframe confluence, and the
//  reading of delta and cumulative volume delta as a measure of buying against selling pressure,
//  are all common knowledge across the trading community and belong to no single author.
//
//  I also acknowledge, and state again in the honest disclosure below, that the buy and sell
//  volume split, and therefore every delta and flow figure in this tool, is an ESTIMATE derived
//  from candle geometry. It is not order book data and it is not true aggressor-side classification.
//  No script built on standard open, high, low, close and volume can produce genuine order flow.
//
//  My original contribution, and what this declaration covers, is the specific code
//  implementation: my own gap detection and filtering, my own multi-timeframe request structure,
//  my own six-factor strength model and weighting, my own confluence merge and bonus, my own
//  mitigation engine, my own flow-bar and label rendering, my own dashboard architecture, and my
//  own presentation layer. Conceptual overlap with other fair value gap tools is therefore
//  unavoidable and expected, but there is no source-code overlap of any kind with any other
//  author's work.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  W H A T   T H I S   I N D I C A T O R   D O E S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  A fair value gap is a three-candle imbalance: the middle candle moves so hard that the first
//  and third candles do not overlap, leaving a price range that never traded efficiently. This
//  tool finds those gaps on three timeframes at once, scores each one for how meaningful it really
//  is, and reports the whole picture through a live dashboard.
//
//  1) FAIR VALUE GAP DETECTION
//     A bullish gap exists when the low of the third candle sits above the high of the first. A
//     bearish gap exists when the high of the third sits below the low of the first. A gap smaller
//     than the configurable ATR-relative minimum is ignored, so only meaningful imbalances survive.
//
//  2) THREE TIMEFRAMES AT ONCE
//     Gaps are found independently on three timeframes of your choosing, defaulting to one, two and
//     four hours, and mapped onto whatever chart you are viewing. A gap that exists only on the
//     fastest timeframe is short-term noise. A gap that exists on the slowest is a level of real
//     significance, and the tool lets you see both without changing charts.
//
//  3) SIX-FACTOR STRENGTH SCORE, 0 TO 10
//     Each gap is scored from six components: the displacement that formed it relative to ATR, how
//     directional the volume was through it, how elevated that volume was against its own average,
//     the net buy-versus-sell dominance, the solidity of the middle candle's body, and absorption,
//     the volume that failed to move price and was left in the wicks. The weighted result is
//     classified PEAK, HIGH, FAIR, SOFT or WEAK.
//
//  4) CONFLUENCE MERGE
//     When gaps from different timeframes overlap, they are fused into a single confluence zone
//     tagged with every timeframe involved, and awarded a bonus, because agreement across
//     timeframes is more reliable than any single one.
//
//  5) MITIGATION
//     When price returns and fills a gap, by touch, by half or in full at your choice, the gap is
//     mitigated and either removed or kept dimmed as history.
//
//  6) FLOW BARS AND STATISTICS
//     Each zone carries two small bars showing the estimated buying and selling share of the
//     volume that formed it, and a label reporting the timeframes involved, the net delta and the
//     relative volume.
//
//  7) DASHBOARD
//     A multi-section panel reports, per timeframe, the count of bullish and bearish gaps and the
//     resulting bias; the strongest zone and the nearest zone above and below price; a flow
//     pressure section with aggregate delta, chart delta, a cumulative delta bias and the active
//     session; and live counts of active, confluent and filled zones.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  H O N E S T   D I S C L O S U R E   O N   M E T H O D
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  I state the following plainly so nothing here is oversold.
//
//  Every delta, flow percentage, absorption reading and cumulative delta figure in this tool is
//  built on an ESTIMATED buy and sell split, derived from where each bar closed within its own
//  range. It is not order book data, it is not real bid and ask classification, and it cannot see
//  which side was the aggressor on any individual trade. This is a long established estimation
//  technique, it is genuinely useful as a directional bias, and it is still an approximation. No
//  indicator built on standard open, high, low, close and volume can do better, and any tool
//  claiming true order flow from those five inputs is overstating what it has.
//
//  The strength score is a weighted model, not a probability. It ranks gaps by how convincingly
//  they formed. It does not promise that a high-scoring gap will hold, and it is not a backtest.
//
//  Read this tool as a structured, multi-timeframe way to rank imbalances and read estimated flow,
//  not as a source of exact order-flow figures.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  L I V E   B E H A V I O U R   A N D   R E P A I N T I N G   S T A T E M E N T
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  A gap is confirmed only once its three candles have closed, so a gap never appears on an
//  unfinished candle and never vanishes from history afterwards. A confirmed gap's boundaries and
//  score are fixed at creation.
//
//  All multi-timeframe requests use lookahead off, so no future higher-timeframe data can reach a
//  past bar. A higher-timeframe gap therefore appears only once its own bar has closed, which is
//  the correct non-repainting behaviour. The dashboard and the mitigation state update live, which
//  is expected: they describe the current state of the market on the most recent bar.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  D I S C L A I M E R
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  This tool is for educational and informational purposes only. It does not constitute financial
//  advice. Trading involves risk; past patterns do not guarantee future results. The delta and
//  flow figures are estimates derived from candle geometry, not real order flow, and the strength
//  score is a ranking model, not a probability. Use proper risk management and consult a licensed
//  financial advisor before trading real capital.
// ==============================================================================================

indicator("SMC OrderFlow FVG", "OF-FVG", overlay = true, max_boxes_count = 500, max_lines_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500, max_bars_back = 1000)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  I N P U T S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
gTf = "=====  TIMEFRAMES  ====="
tfA    = input.timeframe("60",  "Timeframe 1", group = gTf, inline = "a")
tfAon  = input.bool(true, "", group = gTf, inline = "a")
tfB    = input.timeframe("120", "Timeframe 2", group = gTf, inline = "b")
tfBon  = input.bool(true, "", group = gTf, inline = "b")
tfC    = input.timeframe("240", "Timeframe 3", group = gTf, inline = "c")
tfCon  = input.bool(true, "", group = gTf, inline = "c")

gDet = "=====  GAP DETECTION  ====="
atrLen   = input.int(14, "ATR Length", minval = 2, maxval = 200, group = gDet)
minMode  = input.string("ATR Multiple", "Minimum Size Mode", options = ["ATR Multiple", "Percent Of Price"], group = gDet)
minATR   = input.float(0.6, "Minimum Gap (x ATR)", minval = 0.0, maxval = 8, step = 0.1, group = gDet, tooltip = "A gap smaller than this fraction of ATR is ignored, so only meaningful imbalances survive.")
minPct   = input.float(0.10, "Minimum Gap (Percent)", minval = 0.0, maxval = 5, step = 0.01, group = gDet)
maxPerTf = input.int(8, "Max Gaps Per Timeframe", minval = 1, maxval = 30, group = gDet)

gScore = "=====  STRENGTH MODEL  ====="
minStrength = input.float(3.5, "Minimum Strength To Show", minval = 0, maxval = 10, step = 0.5, group = gScore, tooltip = "Gaps scoring below this are tracked but not drawn. Raise it to keep only the strongest imbalances.")
wDisp   = input.float(0.25, "Weight - Displacement",   minval = 0, maxval = 1, step = 0.05, group = gScore)
wDelta  = input.float(0.20, "Weight - Delta Alignment",minval = 0, maxval = 1, step = 0.05, group = gScore)
wRvol   = input.float(0.15, "Weight - Relative Volume",minval = 0, maxval = 1, step = 0.05, group = gScore)
wFlow   = input.float(0.15, "Weight - Flow Dominance", minval = 0, maxval = 1, step = 0.05, group = gScore)
wBody   = input.float(0.15, "Weight - Middle Body",    minval = 0, maxval = 1, step = 0.05, group = gScore)
wAbsorb = input.float(0.10, "Weight - Absorption",     minval = 0, maxval = 1, step = 0.05, group = gScore)
conflBonus = input.float(1.2, "Confluence Bonus (per extra TF)", minval = 0, maxval = 3, step = 0.1, group = gScore)

gConf = "=====  CONFLUENCE  ====="
mergeOn  = input.bool(true, "Merge Overlapping Timeframe Gaps", group = gConf)
mergeATR = input.float(0.5, "Merge Distance (x ATR)", minval = 0.0, maxval = 3, step = 0.1, group = gConf)

gMit = "=====  MITIGATION  ====="
fillMode = input.string("50% Fill", "Fill Rule", options = ["Touch", "50% Fill", "Full Fill"], group = gMit, tooltip = "How much of the gap price must fill before it is mitigated.")
removeFilled = input.bool(false, "Remove Filled Zones", group = gMit, tooltip = "OFF keeps a filled zone dimmed as history. ON removes it.")

gVis = "=====  VISUALS  ====="
showZones = input.bool(true, "Show Zones", group = gVis)
extendR   = input.int(20, "Extend Right (bars)", minval = 0, maxval = 200, group = gVis)
showFlow  = input.bool(true, "Show Flow Bars", group = gVis)
showLbl   = input.bool(true, "Show Stats Label", group = gVis)
showTier  = input.bool(true, "Show Tier Text In Zone", group = gVis)
lblSize   = input.string("Small", "Label Size", options = ["Tiny", "Small", "Normal"], group = gVis)

gDash = "=====  DASHBOARD  ====="
showDash = input.bool(true, "Show Dashboard", group = gDash)
dashPos  = input.string("Top Right", "Position", options = ["Top Right", "Middle Right", "Bottom Right", "Top Left", "Bottom Left"], group = gDash)

gSess = "=====  SESSION READOUT  ====="
sessTz   = input.string("UTC", "Timezone", group = gSess)
sessAsia = input.session("0000-0800", "Asian",   group = gSess)
sessLond = input.session("0700-1600", "London",  group = gSess)
sessNy   = input.session("1200-2100", "New York", group = gSess)

gSty = "=====  STYLE  ====="
colBull  = input.color(#26a69a, "Bullish Gap", group = gSty, inline = "a")
colBear  = input.color(#ef5350, "Bearish Gap", group = gSty, inline = "a")
colConf  = input.color(#f0b90b, "Confluence Tag", group = gSty)
colBuy   = input.color(#26c281, "Buy Flow",  group = gSty, inline = "b")
colSell  = input.color(#e05c5c, "Sell Flow", group = gSty, inline = "b")
zoneTrans= input.int(80, "Zone Transparency", minval = 0, maxval = 100, group = gSty)
mitTrans = input.int(93, "Filled Transparency", minval = 0, maxval = 100, group = gSty)
colDashB = input.color(#0b1020, "Dashboard Background", group = gSty)
colDashT = input.color(#d1d4dc, "Dashboard Text", group = gSty)

string szL = lblSize == "Tiny" ? size.tiny : lblSize == "Normal" ? size.normal : size.small

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  U N I V E R S A L   A C T I V I T Y   +   B U Y / S E L L   S P L I T
//  The split is an estimate from candle geometry, feeding every delta and flow figure. See the
//  disclosure in the header.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
splitBar() =>
    float rng = high - low
    float v   = nz(volume)
    float hasV = ta.cum(v) > 0 ? 1.0 : 0.0
    float tr   = ta.tr(true)
    float ba   = ta.atr(20)
    float eff  = tr > 0 ? math.abs(close - open) / tr : 0.0
    float syn  = ba > 0 ? math.max(0.0, (tr / ba) * (0.55 + 0.45 * eff) * 1000.0) : 0.0
    float use  = hasV > 0 ? v : syn
    float bv   = rng > 0 ? use * (close - low) / rng : use * 0.5
    float sv   = rng > 0 ? use * (high - close) / rng : use * 0.5
    [bv, sv, use, hasV]

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  P E R - T I M E F R A M E   F V G   E N G I N E
//  Evaluated as a function so the identical detection runs on each requested timeframe. It returns
//  the newest gap detected on the closed 3-candle window, its side, its bounds, and the flow data
//  needed to score it. Confirmed on closed bars only.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
fvgEngine() =>
    float a = ta.atr(atrLen)
    [bv0, sv0, v0, hv0] = splitBar()          // middle candle is [1]
    // gap defined by candle [2] (first) and candle [0]=current-close (third)
    float hi1 = high[2]
    float lo1 = low[2]
    float hi3 = high[0]
    float lo3 = low[0]

    float minSize = minMode == "ATR Multiple" ? a * minATR : close * minPct / 100.0

    int   side = 0
    float top  = na
    float bot  = na
    // bullish gap: third low above first high
    if lo3 > hi1 and (lo3 - hi1) >= minSize
        side := 1
        top  := lo3
        bot  := hi1
    // bearish gap: third high below first low
    else if hi3 < lo1 and (lo1 - hi3) >= minSize
        side := -1
        top  := lo1
        bot  := hi3

    // flow measured on the middle (displacement) candle [1]
    float rvol = ta.sma(v0, 20) > 0 ? v0 / ta.sma(v0, 20) : 1.0
    float bodyFrac = (high[1] - low[1]) > 0 ? math.abs(close[1] - open[1]) / (high[1] - low[1]) : 0.0

    [side, top, bot, bv0, sv0, v0, rvol, bodyFrac, a, hv0]

// request each timeframe
[sA, tA_, bA_, bvA, svA, vA, rvA, bfA, atrA, hvA] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tfA, fvgEngine(), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)
[sB, tB_, bB_, bvB, svB, vB, rvB, bfB, atrB, hvB] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tfB, fvgEngine(), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)
[sC, tC_, bC_, bvC, svC, vC, rvC, bfC, atrC, hvC] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tfC, fvgEngine(), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  S T R E N G T H   S C O R E
//  Six dimensionless components combined by weight. No raw price term anywhere.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
scoreGap(int side, float top, float bot, float bv, float sv, float rvol, float bodyFrac, float a) =>
    float tot  = bv + sv
    float disp = a > 0 ? math.min((top - bot) / a / 1.5, 1.0) : 0.0
    float delta = tot > 0 ? (bv - sv) / tot : 0.0
    float align = side == 1 ? math.max(0.0, delta) : math.max(0.0, -delta)   // delta agrees with gap side
    float rv    = math.min(rvol / 2.0, 1.0)
    float flow  = math.abs(delta)
    float body  = bodyFrac
    float absorb= 1.0 - bodyFrac                                             // volume left in wicks
    float wSum  = math.max(wDisp + wDelta + wRvol + wFlow + wBody + wAbsorb, 0.0001)
    float raw   = (disp * wDisp + align * wDelta + rv * wRvol + flow * wFlow + body * wBody + absorb * wAbsorb) / wSum
    math.max(0.0, math.min(10.0, raw * 10.0))

tierOf(float sc) =>
    sc >= 8.0 ? "PEAK" : sc >= 6.5 ? "HIGH" : sc >= 5.0 ? "FAIR" : sc >= 3.5 ? "SOFT" : "WEAK"

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Z O N E   R E G I S T R Y
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
type Gap
    float top
    float bot
    int   side
    int   born
    float score
    float bv
    float sv
    string tftag
    int   tfcount
    bool  filled
    box   bx
    box   fbuy
    box   fsell
    label lb
    label tl

var array<Gap> gaps = array.new<Gap>()

bool newBull = false
bool newBear = false
bool anyFill = false

method wipe(Gap g) =>
    box.delete(g.bx)
    box.delete(g.fbuy)
    box.delete(g.fsell)
    label.delete(g.lb)
    label.delete(g.tl)

tfName(string tf) =>
    int sec = timeframe.in_seconds(tf)
    na(sec) ? tf : sec < 3600 ? str.tostring(sec / 60) + "m" : sec < 86400 ? "H" + str.tostring(sec / 3600) : sec < 604800 ? "D" + str.tostring(sec / 86400) : "W"

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  I N G E S T   N E W   G A P S   F R O M   E A C H   T I M E F R A M E
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ingest(bool on, int side, float top, float bot, float bv, float sv, float rvol, float bodyFrac, float a, string tf, bool isNewBar) =>
    bool madeBull = false
    bool madeBear = false
    if on and isNewBar and side != 0 and not na(top) and not na(bot) and not na(a) and a > 0
        float sc  = scoreGap(side, top, bot, bv, sv, rvol, bodyFrac, a)
        float mid = (top + bot) / 2.0
        float mergeD = a * mergeATR
        string nm = tfName(tf)

        int hit = -1
        if mergeOn and gaps.size() > 0
            for m = 0 to gaps.size() - 1
                Gap g = gaps.get(m)
                if not g.filled and g.side == side and math.abs(((g.top + g.bot) / 2) - mid) <= mergeD
                    hit := m
        if hit >= 0
            Gap g = gaps.get(hit)
            if not str.contains(g.tftag, nm)
                g.tftag := g.tftag + "-" + nm
                g.tfcount += 1
                g.score := math.min(10.0, math.max(g.score, sc) + conflBonus)
            g.top := math.max(g.top, top)
            g.bot := math.min(g.bot, bot)
            g.bv  := g.bv + bv
            g.sv  := g.sv + sv
        else
            Gap g = Gap.new()
            g.top := top
            g.bot := bot
            g.side := side
            g.born := bar_index
            g.score := sc
            g.bv := bv
            g.sv := sv
            g.tftag := nm
            g.tfcount := 1
            g.filled := false
            gaps.push(g)
            if side == 1
                madeBull := true
            else
                madeBear := true

    [madeBull, madeBear]

// detect a fresh higher-timeframe bar so each gap is ingested once
bool nbA = ta.change(time(tfA)) != 0
bool nbB = ta.change(time(tfB)) != 0
bool nbC = ta.change(time(tfC)) != 0

if barstate.isconfirmed
    [mba, mea] = ingest(tfAon, sA, tA_, bA_, bvA, svA, rvA, bfA, atrA, tfA, nbA)
    [mbb, meb] = ingest(tfBon, sB, tB_, bB_, bvB, svB, rvB, bfB, atrB, tfB, nbB)
    [mbc, mec] = ingest(tfCon, sC, tC_, bC_, bvC, svC, rvC, bfC, atrC, tfC, nbC)
    newBull := mba or mbb or mbc
    newBear := mea or meb or mec

    // enforce per-side caps (counting confluence gaps once per side)
    int capTotal = maxPerTf * 3
    while gaps.size() > capTotal
        Gap g = gaps.shift()
        g.wipe()

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  M I T I G A T I O N
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
float chartAtr = ta.atr(atrLen)

if barstate.isconfirmed and gaps.size() > 0
    for m = gaps.size() - 1 to 0
        Gap g = gaps.get(m)
        if not g.filled
            float fillLine = fillMode == "Touch" ? (g.side == 1 ? g.top : g.bot) : fillMode == "Full Fill" ? (g.side == 1 ? g.bot : g.top) : (g.top + g.bot) / 2.0
            bool hit = g.side == 1 ? low <= fillLine : high >= fillLine
            if hit
                g.filled := true
                anyFill := true
                if removeFilled
                    g.wipe()
                    gaps.remove(m)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  C H A R T - T I M E F R A M E   F L O W   ( for the dashboard )
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[cbv, csv, cvol, chv] = splitBar()
float chartDelta = cbv - csv
var float cvd = 0.0
cvd := cvd + chartDelta
float cvdBias = ta.cum(cvol) > 0 ? cvd / ta.cum(cvol) * 100.0 : 0.0
float chartRvol = ta.sma(cvol, 20) > 0 ? cvol / ta.sma(cvol, 20) * 100.0 : 100.0

bool inAsia = not na(time(timeframe.period, sessAsia, sessTz))
bool inLond = not na(time(timeframe.period, sessLond, sessTz))
bool inNy   = not na(time(timeframe.period, sessNy,   sessTz))
string sessTxt = inLond and inNy ? "LDN/NY" : inNy ? "NY" : inLond ? "London" : inAsia ? "Asia" : "Off"

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  A G G R E G A T E S   F O R   T H E   D A S H B O A R D
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
var int   cntActive = 0
var int   cntConf   = 0
var int   cntFilled = 0
var float fvgDelta  = 0.0
var float strongSc  = 0.0
var float strongPx  = na
var string strongTag = "-"
var float nearUpPx  = na
var float nearUpSc  = 0.0
var string nearUpTag = "-"
var float nearDnPx  = na
var float nearDnSc  = 0.0
var string nearDnTag = "-"

// per-timeframe bull/bear counts
var int bullA = 0
var int bearA = 0
var int bullB = 0
var int bearB = 0
var int bullC = 0
var int bearC = 0

countSideForTf(string nm) =>
    int bl = 0
    int br = 0
    if gaps.size() > 0
        for m = 0 to gaps.size() - 1
            Gap g = gaps.get(m)
            if not g.filled and str.contains(g.tftag, nm)
                if g.side == 1
                    bl += 1
                else
                    br += 1
    [bl, br]

if barstate.islast
    cntActive := 0
    cntConf   := 0
    cntFilled := 0
    fvgDelta  := 0.0
    strongSc  := 0.0
    strongPx  := na
    strongTag := "-"
    nearUpPx  := na
    nearUpSc  := 0.0
    nearUpTag := "-"
    nearDnPx  := na
    nearDnSc  := 0.0
    nearDnTag := "-"
    float nearUpD = na
    float nearDnD = na

    if gaps.size() > 0
        for m = 0 to gaps.size() - 1
            Gap g = gaps.get(m)
            if g.filled
                cntFilled += 1
            else
                cntActive += 1
                if g.tfcount > 1
                    cntConf += 1
                fvgDelta += g.bv - g.sv
                if g.score > strongSc
                    strongSc := g.score
                    strongPx := (g.top + g.bot) / 2.0
                    strongTag := g.tftag
                float mid = (g.top + g.bot) / 2.0
                if mid >= close
                    float d = mid - close
                    if na(nearUpD) or d < nearUpD
                        nearUpD := d
                        nearUpPx := mid
                        nearUpSc := g.score
                        nearUpTag := g.tftag
                else
                    float d = close - mid
                    if na(nearDnD) or d < nearDnD
                        nearDnD := d
                        nearDnPx := mid
                        nearDnSc := g.score
                        nearDnTag := g.tftag

    [blA, brA] = countSideForTf(tfName(tfA))
    [blB, brB] = countSideForTf(tfName(tfB))
    [blC, brC] = countSideForTf(tfName(tfC))
    bullA := blA
    bearA := brA
    bullB := blB
    bearB := brB
    bullC := blC
    bearC := brC

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  D R A W   Z O N E S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
if barstate.islast and showZones and gaps.size() > 0
    for m = 0 to gaps.size() - 1
        Gap g = gaps.get(m)
        if g.score >= minStrength or g.tfcount > 1
            color base = g.side == 1 ? colBull : colBear
            int   trans = g.filled ? mitTrans : zoneTrans
            int   right = bar_index + extendR
            int   left  = g.born

            g.wipe()

            g.bx := box.new(left, g.top, right, g.bot, xloc = xloc.bar_index, border_color = color.new(g.tfcount > 1 ? colConf : base, g.filled ? 70 : 40), border_width = g.tfcount > 1 ? 2 : 1, bgcolor = color.new(base, trans))

            if showTier and not g.filled
                box.set_text(g.bx, tierOf(g.score))
                box.set_text_color(g.bx, color.new(base, 20))
                box.set_text_size(g.bx, size.small)
                box.set_text_halign(g.bx, text.align_center)

            // flow bars to the right of the zone
            float tot = g.bv + g.sv
            if showFlow and tot > 0 and not g.filled
                float buyPct = g.bv / tot
                int fx1 = right + 2
                int fx2 = right + 2 + math.max(3, extendR)
                float mid = (g.top + g.bot) / 2.0
                float h = math.max(chartAtr, (g.top - g.bot)) * 0.5
                int wBuy  = math.max(1, int((fx2 - fx1) * buyPct))
                int wSell = math.max(1, int((fx2 - fx1) * (1 - buyPct)))
                g.fbuy  := box.new(fx1, mid + h * 0.15, fx1 + wBuy,  mid - h * 0.15, xloc = xloc.bar_index, border_color = color.new(colBuy, 100), bgcolor = color.new(colBuy, 15))
                g.fsell := box.new(fx1, mid + h * 0.55, fx1 + wSell, mid + h * 0.25, xloc = xloc.bar_index, border_color = color.new(colSell, 100), bgcolor = color.new(colSell, 15))
                g.tl := label.new(fx1 + wBuy, mid - h * 0.15, str.tostring(buyPct * 100, "#.#") + "%", xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_none, textcolor = colBuy, size = size.tiny)

            if showLbl and not g.filled
                float delta = g.bv - g.sv
                string tag = (g.tfcount > 1 ? "CONF " : "") + g.tftag
                string dtxt = "  Δ " + (delta >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(delta, format.volume)
                g.lb := label.new(left, g.side == 1 ? g.top : g.bot, tag + dtxt + "   " + tierOf(g.score) + " " + str.tostring(g.score, "#.#"), xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = g.side == 1 ? label.style_label_lower_left : label.style_label_upper_left, color = color.new(base, 15), textcolor = color.white, size = szL)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  D A S H B O A R D
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
var table dash = na

dashPosition() =>
    dashPos == "Middle Right" ? position.middle_right : dashPos == "Bottom Right" ? position.bottom_right : dashPos == "Top Left" ? position.top_left : dashPos == "Bottom Left" ? position.bottom_left : position.top_right

biasTxt(int bl, int br) =>
    bl > br ? "BULL" : br > bl ? "BEAR" : "FLAT"
biasCol(int bl, int br) =>
    bl > br ? colBull : br > bl ? colBear : color.new(colDashT, 40)

if barstate.islast and showDash
    table.delete(dash)
    dash := table.new(dashPosition(), 4, 17, border_width = 1, border_color = color.new(colDashT, 85), frame_width = 1, frame_color = color.new(colDashT, 75))

    color bgT = color.new(colDashB, 0)
    color bgH = color.new(colDashB, 10)
    color bgR = color.new(colDashB, 20)
    color dim = color.new(colDashT, 45)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 0, "SMC ORDERFLOW FVG  -  MTF", bgcolor = bgT, text_color = colConf, text_size = size.small)
    table.merge_cells(dash, 0, 0, 2, 0)
    table.cell(dash, 3, 0, timeframe.period + "  " + syminfo.ticker, bgcolor = bgT, text_color = dim, text_size = size.tiny)

    // timeframes section
    table.cell(dash, 0, 1, "TIMEFRAMES", bgcolor = bgH, text_color = colConf, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 1, "BULL", bgcolor = bgH, text_color = dim, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 2, 1, "BEAR", bgcolor = bgH, text_color = dim, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 3, 1, "BIAS", bgcolor = bgH, text_color = dim, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 2, tfName(tfA), bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 2, str.tostring(bullA), bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colBull, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 2, 2, str.tostring(bearA), bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colBear, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 3, 2, biasTxt(bullA, bearA), bgcolor = bgR, text_color = biasCol(bullA, bearA), text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 3, tfName(tfB), bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 3, str.tostring(bullB), bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colBull, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 2, 3, str.tostring(bearB), bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colBear, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 3, 3, biasTxt(bullB, bearB), bgcolor = bgR, text_color = biasCol(bullB, bearB), text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 4, tfName(tfC), bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 4, str.tostring(bullC), bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colBull, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 2, 4, str.tostring(bearC), bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colBear, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 3, 4, biasTxt(bullC, bearC), bgcolor = bgR, text_color = biasCol(bullC, bearC), text_size = size.tiny)

    // key zones section
    table.cell(dash, 0, 5, "KEY ZONES", bgcolor = bgH, text_color = colConf, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 5, "PRICE", bgcolor = bgH, text_color = dim, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 2, 5, "TF", bgcolor = bgH, text_color = dim, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 3, 5, "SCORE", bgcolor = bgH, text_color = dim, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 6, "Strongest", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colConf, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 6, na(strongPx) ? "-" : str.tostring(strongPx, format.mintick), bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 2, 6, strongTag, bgcolor = bgR, text_color = dim, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 3, 6, strongSc > 0 ? str.tostring(strongSc, "#.#") + " " + tierOf(strongSc) : "-", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colConf, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 7, "Nearest Up", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colBear, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 7, na(nearUpPx) ? "-" : str.tostring(nearUpPx, format.mintick), bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 2, 7, nearUpTag, bgcolor = bgR, text_color = dim, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 3, 7, nearUpSc > 0 ? str.tostring(nearUpSc, "#.#") : "-", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 8, "Nearest Dn", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colBull, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 8, na(nearDnPx) ? "-" : str.tostring(nearDnPx, format.mintick), bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 2, 8, nearDnTag, bgcolor = bgR, text_color = dim, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 3, 8, nearDnSc > 0 ? str.tostring(nearDnSc, "#.#") : "-", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)

    // flow pressure section
    table.cell(dash, 0, 9, "FLOW PRESSURE", bgcolor = bgH, text_color = colConf, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.merge_cells(dash, 0, 9, 3, 9)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 10, "FVG Net Δ", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 10, str.tostring(fvgDelta, format.volume), bgcolor = bgR, text_color = fvgDelta >= 0 ? colBull : colBear, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 2, 10, "Regime", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 3, 10, fvgDelta >= 0 ? "ACCUM" : "DISTRIB", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = fvgDelta >= 0 ? colBull : colBear, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 11, "Chart Δ", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 11, (chartDelta >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(chartDelta, format.volume), bgcolor = bgR, text_color = chartDelta >= 0 ? colBull : colBear, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 2, 11, "RVOL", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 3, 11, str.tostring(chartRvol, "#") + "%", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 12, "CVD Bias", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 12, str.tostring(cvdBias, "#") + "%", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = cvdBias >= 0 ? colBull : colBear, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 2, 12, "Session", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 3, 12, sessTxt, bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)

    // stats section
    table.cell(dash, 0, 13, "STATS", bgcolor = bgH, text_color = colConf, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.merge_cells(dash, 0, 13, 3, 13)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 14, "Active / Confluence", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 14, str.tostring(cntActive) + " / " + str.tostring(cntConf), bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 2, 14, "Filled", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 3, 14, str.tostring(cntFilled), bgcolor = bgR, text_color = dim, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 15, "Min Strength", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 15, str.tostring(minStrength, "#.#") + "/10", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 2, 15, "Merge", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 3, 15, mergeOn ? "on" : "off", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = mergeOn ? colBull : dim, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 16, "Fill Rule", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 16, fillMode, bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 2, 16, "Activity", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 3, 16, chv > 0 ? "Real" : "Synth", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = chv > 0 ? colBull : colConf, text_size = size.tiny)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  A L E R T S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
alertcondition(newBull, "OF-FVG - New Bullish Gap", "SMC OrderFlow FVG: a new bullish fair value gap formed on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(newBear, "OF-FVG - New Bearish Gap", "SMC OrderFlow FVG: a new bearish fair value gap formed on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(anyFill, "OF-FVG - Gap Filled", "SMC OrderFlow FVG: a fair value gap was filled on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")

if newBull
    alert("OF-FVG New Bullish Gap - " + syminfo.ticker + " " + timeframe.period, alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if newBear
    alert("OF-FVG New Bearish Gap - " + syminfo.ticker + " " + timeframe.period, alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if anyFill
    alert("OF-FVG Gap Filled - " + syminfo.ticker + " " + timeframe.period, alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  D A T A   W I N D O W   O U T P U T S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
plot(cntActive,  "Active Gaps",     color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)
plot(cntConf,    "Confluence Gaps", color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)
plot(fvgDelta,   "FVG Net Delta",   color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)
plot(chartDelta, "Chart Delta",     color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)
plot(cvdBias,    "CVD Bias %",      color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)
